const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"研究问题",en:"Research question"},body:{zh:"Hansen提出检验预测模型是否相对基准具有优越预测能力的程序，并处理候选模型比较问题。 阅读时先把它理解为一个被界定的问题，而不是可以脱离样本、时间和制度环境的结论。",en:"“A Test for Superior Predictive Ability” frames a bounded research question. Read the stated question together with the named sample, dates, and institutional setting rather than treating it as a conclusion that automatically travels to another market or period."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1198/073500105000000063",label:{zh:"Journal of Business & Economic Statistics (2005) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Business & Economic Statistics (2005) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"研究设计",en:"Research design"},body:{zh:"公开描述将多个模型的损失差放进统一检验框架，关注基准是否被至少一个候选稳定超越。 这说明比较对象、观察窗口和对照关系是研究合同的一部分；改变其中任何一项，都可能改变所检验的命题。",en:"For “A Test for Superior Predictive Ability”, the source describes a deliberate comparison, observation window, and control relation. Those choices are part of its research contract: changing one can change the proposition being tested, even when the method label remains the same."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1198/073500105000000063",label:{zh:"Journal of Business & Economic Statistics (2005) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Business & Economic Statistics (2005) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"数据与时点",en:"Data and timing"},body:{zh:"必须先定义预测目标、损失函数、预测时点、滚动或扩展窗口以及全部候选模型的输出。 数据字段、可得时点和样本筛选需要与原始研究分开记录，不能仅凭同名变量或最终修订数据就视为可比。",en:"For “A Test for Superior Predictive Ability”, keep the fields, their availability timing, and the sample filters separate from the original study. A same-named variable, later-revised database, or matching end-of-period date is not automatically a comparable input."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1198/073500105000000063",label:{zh:"Journal of Business & Economic Statistics (2005) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Business & Economic Statistics (2005) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"如何理解结果",en:"How to read the result"},body:{zh:"方法帮助区分某个样本内赢家与在多模型比较下仍有证据支持的预测优势。 它支持的是该来源所描述的经验或理论关系；它本身不把相关性、模型拟合或历史表现升级为因果、可执行性或未来保证。",en:"For “A Test for Superior Predictive Ability”, the source supports only the empirical or theoretical relation it describes. It does not turn association, model fit, or historical performance into causality, a directly executable procedure, or a guarantee about subsequent outcomes."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1198/073500105000000063",label:{zh:"Journal of Business & Economic Statistics (2005) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Business & Economic Statistics (2005) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"复核清单",en:"Replication checks"},body:{zh:"保持基准模型固定，保存候选集合、预测误差序列和依赖处理方式，并避免测试后再收缩候选池。 在做后续分析前，应把这些选择写入版本化的研究记录，并保留原始来源链接与访问日期。",en:"Before extending “A Test for Superior Predictive Ability”, record its sample, timing, construction choices, and source edition in a versioned note. Keep the primary-source link and access date so a later reader can distinguish a changed definition from a changed result."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1198/073500105000000063",label:{zh:"Journal of Business & Economic Statistics (2005) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Business & Economic Statistics (2005) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"适用边界",en:"Scope boundary"},body:{zh:"该条导读引用 Journal of Business & Economic Statistics (2005)。预测统计优势与投资收益、交易容量或跨市场迁移能力是不同问题。 若需要量化结论、参数、表格或稳健性检验，请回到原文并单独核对版本、附录与样本定义。",en:"This guide cites Journal of Business & Economic Statistics (2005) for “A Test for Superior Predictive Ability”. Its public description defines the boundary. For numerical conclusions, parameters, tables, or robustness tests, return to the original and separately verify the edition, appendices, and sample definitions."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1198/073500105000000063",label:{zh:"Journal of Business & Economic Statistics (2005) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Business & Economic Statistics (2005) · source description"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"本文只整理“A Test for Superior Predictive Ability”所公开说明的研究问题与设计边界，不构成收益预测、交易规则或全文复现。预测统计优势与投资收益、交易容量或跨市场迁移能力是不同问题。",en:"This guide only organizes the publicly described question and design of “A Test for Superior Predictive Ability”. It is not a return forecast, trading rule, or full-text replication. The source's stated scope remains controlling."}};export{e as default};
